  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ONTARIO QUEBEC &amp; ATLANTIC: PROTECTING WE</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Project activities will result in securement of 2,975 acres, enhancement of 400 acres, management of 71,850 acres previously secured, and stewardship activities of 550 acres of migratory bird habitat in Ontario, Quebec and Atlantic provinces of Canada. A number of EHJV migratory waterfowl species such as Common Eider, American Black Duck, Mallard, Harlequin Duck, Canada Goose, Long-tailed Duck, and Barrows Goldeneye will benefit from the protection and enhancement activities of this project.</narrative>
  </description>
